            <p>This route is especially popular because it combines reliable rail service with direct connectivity through the Virginia Piedmont and into the heart of the Northeast Corridor. The presence of multiple Amtrak services means you can travel between these cities with comfortable onboard amenities, making it a strong alternative to driving on I-64 and I-95. </p>
